      "note": "Noun takes pasture. Corrected: the supplied on no longer joins this unit. מִרְעֶה is the bare complement of תִּרְעֶינָה with no preposition and no object marker of its own, so the English verb's valency is what licenses the word and rule 44 puts it on the verb, as EZK.34.18 does for the same verb. Competing reading: rule 33, reading מִרְעֶה as an adverbial accusative of place whose own case-function licenses the on; that reading was taken here before and is set aside because a complement of רעה is what the verb governs, not an accusative of manner or direction like rule 33's as a bird.",
