  "ref": "EZK.34.14",
  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected at chapter reconciliation: the on of on fat pasture moves from מִרְעֶה to the verb. The noun is the bare complement of תִּרְעֶינָה, carrying neither a preposition nor an object marker, so the supplied on is licensed by the English verb's valency and joins the verb's unit under rule 44, discontinuous around fat pasture under rule 25 and still headed on feed. Rule 33 governs a function word supplied for an adverbial accusative, which this is not; the competing reading is recorded in the unit for מִרְעֶה.",
    "This brings the verse into line with EZK.34.18, where הַמִּרְעֶה הַטּוֹב תִּרְעוּ gives upon to the verb and מִשְׁקַע מַיִם תִּשְׁתּוּ gives it of, and with EZK.34.15, where אֶרְעֶה צֹאנִי gives of to the verb's recasting.",
    "Unchanged: where a Hebrew preposition is present it still takes the English word, so בְּמִרְעֶה טּוֹב keeps with on the ב and אֶל הָרֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל keeps upon on אֶל, under rule 44's first limit."
  ]
